    "types.<type>.recipes: one recipe per entry, id grindless:<type>/<name>. itemsIn / itemsOut: { id, count }; kept: items needed in a bus but never used up; fluidsIn / fluidsOut: { id, amount }; charge: fluids needed in a hatch but never drained (GTM's notConsumableFluid). eut and duration are written as the final figures.",
    "pyroprocessing: UV hull voltage (524,288 EU/t) x the tuned ticks. accelerator_driven: a generator type; eut is the EU/t GIVEN (the script writes it as -eut). 1,572,864 EU/t = 3 A UV, and the type stays out of lib/generators.js TYPES so the recipe is not doubled (docs/research/uv-s0.md, S0-6).",
    "chemical_reactor: rows of GTM's chemical reactor keyed by our fluids (line 3 and the salt charge)."
